## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-frontend` rates these patterns by this table. Change a row here, never in a reviewer.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| `makeObservable(this)` or an observable decorator missing (Rule 1) | the field is read by a component or a computed | `major` | a plain field nothing observes (injected props, config) |
| Derived value as a plain method instead of `@computed` (Rule 1) | its callers recompute it in render | `minor` | a selector that takes arguments (`getById`) |
| Mutation outside an action: after `await`, in a callback (Rule 2) | always | `major`; `blocker` where the interleaving corrupts persisted state | a direct mutation in a public sync `@action.bound` method |
| API/IO in a public action body instead of a private method (Rule 3) | always | `minor`; `major` with a named defect it causes | — |
| `@action.bound` on a private method; an inter-store callback without `private` (Rule 3) | always | `minor` | a method a component calls |
| Loading flag not cleared on error, no `finally`, or no `disposed` guard after `await` (Rule 4) | a named failure or unmount leaves the flag set or writes to a disposed store | `major` | — |
| `catch (err: any)` or untyped (Rule 4) | always | rated by `error-handling` | — |
| Reaction or child store never disposed (Rule 5) | always | `major` | a store that lives as long as the app, stated |
| Observable collection reassigned (Rule 6) | a holder of the old reference stops updating, named | `major`; else `minor` | `@observable.ref` replaced whole |
| Deep `@observable` on a list only ever replaced whole, or on a large external object (Rule 6) | always | `minor` | — |
| Two-way sync with no equality guard (Rule 7) | always | `blocker` when a named trigger reaches the loop and the render dies; `major` for a reachable hang; `info` with no path | a guard in either direction |
| Truthy guard on a value that may be cleared (Rule 7) | the cleared value is valid input, named | `major` | a field that can never be falsy |
| Component calls `store.loadX()` or a child store's `init()` in an effect (Rule 8) | always | `minor`; `major` with a named defect | the `onMount()`/`onUnmount()` bridge |
| `public` keyword, member order (Rule 3, member order) | always | `minor` | — |
